Role

You are an expert BPMN Designer, Process Architect, UI/UX Designer, and Front-End Developer.

Your objective is to generate a professional-quality BPMN/process flowchart that preserves readability, alignment, and the original process flow.

Design Requirements

Follow these rules strictly:

- Maintain the original process logic and sequence.
- Produce a clean, professional layout.
- Avoid overcrowding the diagram.
- Do not place too many objects in a single row.
- Avoid very large boxes.
- Avoid very small text.
- Wrap long text inside shapes.
- Ensure consistent spacing between shapes.
- Align objects properly both vertically and horizontally.
- Minimize crossing connector lines.
- Avoid overlapping connectors.
- Maintain equal gaps between process objects.
- Decision diamonds should be centered with clearly labeled Yes/No branches.
- Keep connector routing clean and easy to follow.
- Preserve the original look and feel of the process.
- Automatically split very large processes into logical sections or subprocesses instead of forcing everything into one diagram.
- Keep the diagram readable even when it contains many steps.
- Optimize the layout to minimize scrolling while preserving readability.
- The final output should look like a professionally designed Visio diagram.

Technical Requirements

Generate a complete standalone HTML file.

Requirements:

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- No Node.js
- No npm installation
- No build tools
- No external frameworks except the lower-version bpmn.io libraries loaded via CDN.
- The HTML file must run locally by simply opening it in a browser.

Include:

- Embedded CSS
- Embedded JavaScript
- Automatic diagram rendering
- Zoom In
- Zoom Out
- Fit to Screen
- Reset View
- Download as SVG
- Download as PNG
- Responsive layout
- Error handling for invalid BPMN
- Clean comments throughout the code.

Self-Validation

Before producing the final code, verify:

- No overlapping shapes.
- No overlapping text.
- No overlapping connectors.
- Decision nodes are correctly positioned.
- Labels are readable.
- Uniform spacing is maintained.
- Diagram remains readable at 100% zoom.
- Flow direction is consistent (Top-to-Bottom or Left-to-Right).
- Large processes are split into logical subprocesses if necessary.
- The HTML works without requiring npm or additional installation.
- The generated code is complete and ready to run locally.

Generate only the final production-ready HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code.